{"name":"Tribeca","hex":"#a4918d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tribeca","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A region of lower-west Manhattan, New York City, New York, United States; the Triangle Below Canal Street."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tribeca"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tribeca","blocks":[{"text":"Tribeca, originally written as TriBeCa, is a neighborhood in Lower Manhattan in New York City. Its name is a syllabic abbreviation of \"Triangle Below Canal\". The \"triangle\" is bounded by Canal Street, West Street, Broadway, and Chambers Street. By the 2010s, a common marketing tactic was to extend Tribeca's southern boundary to either Vesey or Murray Streets to increase the appeal of property listings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Tribeca%2C_New_York_%2851521771723%29.jpg/330px-Tribeca%2C_New_York_%2851521771723%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tribeca"},{"title":"TriBeCa (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"TriBeCa is a television drama anthology series created by David J. Burke and co-produced with Robert De Niro and Jane Rosenthal for TriBeCa Productions in 1993 that aired on the Fox Network. The series theme song, \"Keep It Going,\" was performed by the alternative hip hop artist Me Phi Me."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TriBeCa_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Textile_Building%2C_Tribeca_Historic_District_%2815_October_2005%29.jpg/500px-Textile_Building%2C_Tribeca_Historic_District_%2815_October_2005%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Textile_Building%2C_Tribeca_Historic_District_%2815_October_2005%29.jpg/500px-Textile_Building%2C_Tribeca_Historic_District_%2815_October_2005%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Textile Building (1901) in the Tribeca Historic District","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATextile_Building%2C_Tribeca_Historic_District_(15_October_2005).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Radio_Row%2C_Cortlandt_Street%2C_Manhattan_%28NYPL_b13668355-482561%29.jpg/500px-Radio_Row%2C_Cortlandt_Street%2C_Manhattan_%28NYPL_b13668355-482561%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Radio_Row%2C_Cortlandt_Street%2C_Manhattan_%28NYPL_b13668355-482561%29.jpg/1280px-Radio_Row%2C_Cortlandt_Street%2C_Manhattan_%28NYPL_b13668355-482561%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Radio_Row%2C_Cortlandt_Street%2C_Manhattan_%28NYPL_b13668355-482561%29.jpg/500px-Radio_Row%2C_Cortlandt_Street%2C_Manhattan_%28NYPL_b13668355-482561%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Radio Row\", seen here in 1934, was displaced by the building of the World Trade Center. (Photo by Berenice Abbott)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARadio_Row-Berenice_Abbott.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/American_Thread_Wbwy_jeh.JPG/500px-American_Thread_Wbwy_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/American_Thread_Wbwy_jeh.JPG/1280px-American_Thread_Wbwy_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/American_Thread_Wbwy_jeh.JPG/500px-American_Thread_Wbwy_jeh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American Thread Building","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmerican_Thre